            "transcript": "sleep is very important for our health but there are many ideas about it that are not entirely true many people say you should sleep at fixed hours to get enough rest but that isn't always necessary according to science our bodies can adjust to different sleep schedules so it really depends on the individual another common belief is that you should always sleep on a bed instead of a hard floor but this is questionable what everyone agrees on and what studies show is that blocking out light and noise can help improve sleep quality darkness helps our body produce melatonin which is the hormone that makes us feel sleepy while silence allows us to rest better some say that sleep is getting worse for people today but there is no solid proof to support this claim critics often point fingers at the younger generation for their unhealthy sleep patterns but this is sometimes unfair what we can agree on is that the media tends to overemphasize the subject making it seem more serious than it really is in the end finding what works best for you is key to getting a good night's sleep",
